        "wait_and_handle_event": 1
      },
      "interpretation": "Measured with the committed sidecar config and enable_fpu=True. Enabling the VFP coprocessor (FPEXC.EN) removed the earlier UC_ERR_INSN_INVALID at 0x101bd0 on `vmov.i32 q8,#0`, extending the run from 71 to 275 instructions and from 6 to 21 boundary calls, and reaching wait_and_handle_event - the timer/event path cases 5-6 need. The run now faults at 0x102090 on `ldr r3,[r3,#0xd0]`: the preceding `ldr r3,[r4,r3]` resolves a .got slot (0x2f7564) holding 0x3787dc, the sp_camera symbol in .bss. sp_camera is populated at runtime by camera initialisation, so its file value is zero and the dereference yields 0. That is a runtime-state gap, not a decoding failure: the instruction decodes fine and the memory it addresses was never provided.",
      "superseded": "Two earlier measurements are superseded. (1) 33 instructions / UC_ERR_WRITE_UNMAPPED at 0x101b38: measured before .got/.data were seeded, and reproduced exactly when POLARIS_FIRMWARE_ROOT is unset. (2) 71 instructions / UC_ERR_INSN_INVALID at 0x101bd0: recorded as a terminal VFP engine limit, but that was a misdiagnosis. Unicorn exposes UC_ARM_REG_FPEXC and setting bit 30 makes the same vmov execute with correct semantics (Q8 becomes 0). The fault was uninitialised CPU state in the harness, not an engine limit. It was also reported as result=unsupported_instruction because every UcError was classified that way; memory faults now report result=memory_fault."
    },
